    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0585" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 War Credits/698</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Greek Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sicilianos</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-14">June 14, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of June 8, enclosing a statement of the amount due from the
                    Greek Government up to July 1, 1935,<anchor n="25" xml:id="d402-f1"/> under the
                    provisions of Part I of the Debt Agreement of May 10, 1929, and of the
                    Moratorium Agreement of May 24, 1932.</p>
                <p>The Greek Government has taken note with appreciation of the renewed assurance of
                    the United States Government to discuss, through diplomatic channels, their
                    proposals in regard to the settlement of the debts.</p>
                <p>The Greek Government wish to state that they will resume negotiations whenever
                    circumstances will indicate satisfactory results, the situation at the present
                    time not being, to their regret, appropriate for the resumption of
                    discussions.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed>D. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sicilianos</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
